        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="header-title" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CNP · Access matrix · what the segregation plan and the portal roles change&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=24;fontColor=#0f172a;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="30" width="3534" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="header-sub" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#1e293b&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;One row per identity, one column per resource by access plane, the CMP portal included. A cell shows the level after the plan, and what the plan changed to get there.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;Team accounts develop the platform: broad on purpose during the MVP, like break-glass accounts used daily (G21). Segregation applies to the platform&amp;#39;s own identities, its users and the shared demo accounts, one per identity.&lt;br&gt;Read a row: everything an identity can do. Read a column: who can touch a resource. A workload column touched by another project&amp;#39;s identity is a leak.&lt;br&gt;Not verified: the policy of the CMP&amp;#39;s Vault token (G15, drawn as the root token), the scope of its Cloudflare token (G16), the members&amp;#39; GitHub base permission (G17, main is unprotected: checked) and who holds Cloudflare super admin, drawn as the platform admin. GCP project roles (G22), drawn as the platform admin.&lt;br&gt;Plan phases: P1 root accounts and audit trail, P2 CMP rights, P3 tenant isolation and GitOps protection, P4 cloud accounts.&lt;br&gt;Portal lots (CNP-228): L1 authorization holes, L2 Keycloak groups, L3 roles read from Keycloak by the portal, L4 Grafana and Argo CD, L5 cleanup. The same identities hold the platform and the portal.&lt;br&gt;Out of scope: a token issued to another realm client was accepted by the portal API (closed in L1). It carried its user&amp;#39;s rights, so it changes no cell.&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="74" width="3534" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
